      {
        "id": "N004",
        "kind": "internal",
        "statement": "For every 0<=sigma<=1, tau>0, t0>=0 and mean-zero f_j in H^sigma, Rem_(t0,tau) has a unique bounded trilinear extension with ||Rem_(t0,tau)(f_1,f_2,f_3)||_2<=C_sigma*tau^(1+sigma)*product_j||f_j||_(H^sigma), uniformly in t0,tau and Fourier support. In the nonzero interaction a+b+c=k, d=-k, the multiplier obeys |eta_tau(3ab(a+b),3kc(a+b))|/(|k||abc|^sigma)<=6^(1-sigma)*18^sigma*tau^sigma/N3(a,b,c,-k). The same estimates hold with any additional interaction multiplier of modulus <=1, including restrictions to Phi=0 or Phi!=0. In particular if 0<sigma<=1, 0<tau<=1, w in mean-zero H^sigma, f in mean-zero L^2, ||w||_(H^sigma)<=M0 and delta=||f-w||_2<=1, then ||Rem_(t0,tau)(f,f,f)||_2<=C_(sigma,M0)*tau*(tau^sigma+delta), with no Sobolev hypothesis on f.",
