      {
        "id": "N006",
        "kind": "internal",
        "statement": "With normalized norms, for every interval I=[a,b] with 0<=a<=b<=a+1 and continuous piecewise smooth mean-zero paths f_j, ||Ctri_I(f_1,f_2,f_3)||_2<=C|I|product_j||f_j||_(X(I))+C||f_i||_(L^infinity(I;H^(-pstar)))product_(j!=i)||f_j||_(L^infinity(I;L^2)), for each slot i=1,2,3. For time-independent mean-zero H^sigma inputs, 0<=sigma<=1, ||Ctri_I(f_1,f_2,f_3)||_2<=C_sigma|I|^sigma product_j||f_j||_(H^sigma). For 0<gamma<=1 set a_gamma=1/2-gamma when gamma<1/2, a_gamma=1/8 when gamma=1/2, and a_gamma=0 when gamma>1/2. Then a_gamma in [0,1), ||f*g||_2<=C_gamma||f||_(H^gamma)||g||_(H^(a_gamma)). For every M0>=0, mean-zero w with ||w||_(H^gamma)<=M0, 0<tau<=1, a>=0, and a<=t<=a+tau, ||Fstage_(a,t)(w)||_(H^(a_gamma))<=C_(gamma,M0)*tau^gamma and ||Fstage_(a,t)(w)||_(H^(1+gamma))<=C_(gamma,M0). Constants are uniform in a,t,tau and Fourier support. Ctri and stages extend by their stated bounds.",
