        {
          "id": "S001",
          "text": "Fix the local a,tau,M0,f,w, and assume L1: ||w||_(H^gamma)<=M0 and delta=||f-w||_2<=1. H002 gives 0<gamma<=1, hence q=tau^gamma+delta<=2 and ||f||_2<=M0+1. Take the tuple from Interp and the exponent a_gamma from N006. By the endpoint formula in N005, F(t)=(1/6)[J_s(f,f)]_a^t. The J:H^0 times H^0->H^1 bound gives sup||F||_(H^1)<=C_(gamma,M0). Expanding J(f,f)-J(w,w) as J(f-w,f)+J(w,f-w) gives sup||F-Fstage_(a,t)(w)||_(H^1)<=C_(gamma,M0)*delta. Since a_gamma<1, N006 now yields sup(||F||_(H^(a_gamma))+||F||_2)<=C_(gamma,M0)*q. Also z=f+F has bounded L^2 norm and z'=F'=(1/2)B_t(f,f), whose H^(-pstar) norm is bounded by N005, so ||z||_X<=C_(gamma,M0).",
